               <lb n="22" xml:id="trl-p1-l22"/>bwlcyn-pylwcˈ gwpṭˈ pyṭʾk YḤWWNyt MH ZK CBW PWN dʾṭgwšnsp̄ˈ
               <lb n="23" xml:id="trl-p1-l23"/>W ʿLH-šʾn GBRʾ shṭ-š wlhlʾn QDM ḤNḤṬWNd  wcyl W dʾṭwblyh ʾyṭwnˈ ʿBYDWNtny
               <lb n="24" xml:id="trl-p1-l24"/>ZK PWN bwlcyn-pylwcˈ ʾp̄ycymyh lʾd W PWN lʾs Y dʾṭsṭʾn ʿL
               <lb n="25" xml:id="trl-p1-l25"/>ʾp̄ymwsṭyh YḤMṬWNʾṭ ḤṬ cym ZK ḆYN Y plmʾn ʾyl ʾdwynkˈ ʾp̄ẕʾdyk (26)
               <lb n="26" xml:id="trl-p1-l26"/>YḤBWNṭˈ PWN cym Y MNʿDM gwweʾl Wlwšnˈ PWN pshwˈ YKṬYBWN dʾṭgwšnsp̄ˈ-c
               <lb n="27" xml:id="trl-p1-l27"/>plmʾyṭ GBRʾ gwpṭnˈ W pṭkʾlṭnˈ Y QDM ZK CBW [lʾd] LWṬH bwlcyn-pylwcˈ ʿL ZK GBRʾ
               <lb n="28" xml:id="trl-p1-l28"/>LʾWḤL wsydy ʿḆYDWNtny nʾmkˈ BYRḤ whwmnˈ QDM ŠNṬ I-C IIII W YWM wlhlʾnˈ
               <lb n="29" xml:id="trl-p1-l29"/>plmwṭˈ krṭnˈ
               <lb n="30" xml:id="trl-p1-l30"/>ʿL hcʾlʾnwšʾḇyˈʾṭ ʾclmykṭwm ʾḤ hlṭzʾṭˈ nc
               <lb n="31" xml:id="trl-p1-l31"/>wndʾṭhwlšyṭˈ Y plšwʾlgl lṭˈ
            </ab>
         </div>
         <div type="transcription" xml:lang="pal">
            <ab xml:id="MP1025_trc-p1">
               <lb n="1" xml:id="trc-p1-l1"/>A1 ō hazār-anōšayād āzarmīgtom brād Xradzād namāz
               <lb n="2" xml:id="trc-p1-l2"/>A2 Windād-Xw aršēd ī Parišwārgar rad A3 drōd ud harw farroxīh pad
               <lb n="3" xml:id="trc-p1-l3"/>xw adāy bawād ◯ B Burzēn-Pērōz [ī] dibīr ī Farroxgušnasp pus
               <lb n="4" xml:id="trc-p1-l4"/>ī az *Haspīn-raz deh ī pad xānag ī Dēl-Dēlān ī pad tan
               <lb n="5" xml:id="trc-p1-l5"/>abāg payr(ā)[s]tag-nigār pad garzišn pēš man āmad B1 Burzēn-Pērōz
               <lb n="6" xml:id="trc-p1-l6"/>pādrōzag pad ān pēšag ud hušnūdīh xwāstan kū ēwēn būd
               <lb n="7" xml:id="trc-p1-l7"/>andar ēn ēw Dādgušnasp nām-ēw *Ātars pus abāg Yazd nām-ēw
               <lb n="8" xml:id="trc-p1-l8"/>brād ud Rāstdād nām-ēw Wištāsp pus ud Yazdsar nām-ēw Dēlāzād pus ī
               <lb n="9" xml:id="trc-p1-l9"/>az ān *Haspīn-raz deh pad stahm ud xrōst zan ēw *Dēzā
               <lb n="10" xml:id="trc-p1-l10"/>nām ī pādixšāyīhā Burzēn-Pērōz zan az tan payrāyag ud ĵāmag
               <lb n="11" xml:id="trc-p1-l11"/>ud duzīdag ī pad mašk arz s(atēr) 500 hā̂mist abar wišāyēnd
               <lb n="12" xml:id="trc-p1-l12"/>ud apparēnd gyāg gyāg ud ān ayāragīhā pad ēk ī kas kas zāyistan
               <lb n="13" xml:id="trc-p1-l13"/>bē agar abar ān xīr framūd mard mard xwāstan ud pad
               <lb n="14" xml:id="trc-p1-l14"/>abēmustīh ī Burzēn-Pērōz wizīr ud dādwarīh kardan az man ō xwadāy
               <lb n="15" xml:id="trc-p1-l15"/>nāmag bewēd enyā Burzēn-Pērōz ō abēmustīh maden nē
               <lb n="16" xml:id="trc-p1-l16"/>sāxtan ud must būd ud pad ān tis framān dād pēš man (pa)ssox 
               <lb n="17" xml:id="trc-p1-l17"/>agar ast ēn tis ēdōn čiyōn Burzēn-Pērōz garzēd pad ān
               <lb n="18" xml:id="trc-p1-l18"/>ud awēšān mard ēdōn frāz frēstādan nē sazēd ◯ B2 xwadāy
               <lb n="19" xml:id="trc-p1-l19"/>čiyōn Burzēn-Pērōz pad ēwēnag garzēd ēd xīr rāy Dādgušnasp
               <lb n="20" xml:id="trc-p1-l20"/>ud awēšān mard be būdan ud saxwan az-iš āšnūd ēstād tis gōwizār
               <lb n="21" xml:id="trc-p1-l21"/>awēšān ud pad-iš ō gōšān rasīd agar pad ēwēnag ī
               <lb n="22" xml:id="trc-p1-l22"/>Burzēn-Pērōz guft paydāg bawēd čē ān xīr pad Dādgušnasp
               <lb n="23" xml:id="trc-p1-l23"/>ud awēšān mard saxt-īš Wahrām abar nihēnd wizīr ud dādwarīh ēdōn *kunēnd
               <lb n="24" xml:id="trc-p1-l24"/>ān pad Burzēn-Pērōz abēčimīh rāy ud pad rāh ī dādestān ō
               <lb n="25" xml:id="trc-p1-l25"/>abēmustīh rasād agar čim ān andar ī framān ayār ēwēnag abzāyīg
               <lb n="26" xml:id="trc-p1-l26"/>dād pad čim ī tis gōwizār ud rōšn pad passox nibēs Dādgušnasp-iz
               <lb n="27" xml:id="trc-p1-l27"/>framāyēd mard guftan ud pahikārdan ī abar ān xīr [rāy] abāg Burzēn-Pērōz ō ān mard 
               <lb n="28" xml:id="trc-p1-l28"/>abāz wisē kardan Bz nāmag māh Wahman abar sāl 104 ud rōz Wahrām
               <lb n="29" xml:id="trc-p1-l29"/>framūd kardan
               <lb n="30" xml:id="trc-p1-l30"/>C1 ō hazār-anōšayād āzarmīgtom brād Xradzād namāz
               <lb n="31" xml:id="trc-p1-l31"/>C2 Windād-Xwaršēd ī Parišwārgar rad
            </ab>
         </div>
         <div type="translation" xml:lang="de">
            <ab xml:id="MP1025_trans-p1">
               <lb n="1" xml:id="trans-p1-l1"/>A1 To thousand-fold remembered very honoured brother Xradzād, reverence!
               <lb n="2" xml:id="trans-p1-l2"/>A2 Windād-Xw aršēd, the Parišwārgar rad, well-being and all happiness for You
               <lb n="3" xml:id="trans-p1-l3"/>Sir, shall be! B1 Burzēn-Pērōz, the scribe, son of Farroxgušnasp
               <lb n="4" xml:id="trans-p1-l4"/>from the village of *Haspīn-raz in the district of Dēl-Dēlān personally
               <lb n="5" xml:id="trans-p1-l5"/>together with the *painter of adornments* came before me because of a complaint (saying:) B1 (that) Burzēn-Pērōz
               <lb n="6" xml:id="trans-p1-l6"/>would request to being granted a period of grace for that business and (also) satisfaction that (is) legally binding
               <lb n="7" xml:id="trans-p1-l7"/>regarding the following (case): one Dādgušnasp by name, son of *Ātars, together with one Yazd by name,
               <lb n="8" xml:id="trans-p1-l8"/>brother, and one Rāstdād, son of Wištāsp, ane one Yazdsar, son of Dēlāzād,
               <lb n="9" xml:id="trans-p1-l9"/>from the village of *Haspīn-raz by (an act of) violence and shouting one wife, Dēzā
               <lb n="10" xml:id="trans-p1-l10"/>by name, the pādixšāy-wife of Burzēn-Pērōz, from her personal belongings jewellery and goblet(s)
               <lb n="11-12" xml:id="trans-p1-l11-12"/>and how they would open the bag worth a total of 500 staters and carry away the stolen things, (therefore it is necessary) to ask in every place and to check the registers of every single person,
               <lb n="13-14" xml:id="trans-p1-l13-14"/>—unless on that matter he ordered (it already)—to summon every single man and for satisfaction of Burzēn-Pērōz to make a decision and judgement from me to You, Sir,
               <lb n="15-16" xml:id="trans-p1-l15-16"/>this (is the purpose of this) letter as otherwise it will not be possible that Burzēn-Pērōz would come to contentment and complaint still remains and regarding that matter having been ordered, (give) me an answer.
               <lb n="17" xml:id="trans-p1-l17"/>If this matter is such as Burzēn-Pērōz complains for him
               <lb n="18" xml:id="trans-p1-l18"/>and the (other) men to send further is not suitable. B2 Sir,
               <lb n="19" xml:id="trans-p1-l19"/>if Burzēn-Pērōz is still complaining in form because of this property Dādgušnasp
               <lb n="20" xml:id="trans-p1-l20"/>and those (other) men and his statement has been heard
               <lb n="21" xml:id="trans-p1-l21"/>if it becomes evident (line 22), in this way as
               <lb n="22" xml:id="trans-p1-l22"/>Burzēn-Pērōz stated that this property belongs to Dādgušnasp
               <lb n="23" xml:id="trans-p1-l23"/>and those men, when (the day of Wahrām has passed, should reach at a decision and should give a judgement
               <lb n="24" xml:id="trans-p1-l24"/>this for Burzēn-Pērōz because of the groundlessness and by way of a process
               <lb n="25" xml:id="trans-p1-l25"/>Will result in satisfaction. If there is proof therein that is also written that order that it be registered in an additional manner
               <lb n="26" xml:id="trans-p1-l26"/>Concerning the proof of this case write this explicitly and clearly in your answer, also Dādgušnasp
               <lb n="27" xml:id="trans-p1-l27"/>you should order to name the men and to take a legal action against those who (are involved) in that manner with Burzēn-Pērōz
               <lb n="28" xml:id="trans-p1-l28"/>to restore (it/them) to the man (preceding line). Bz The letter month Wahman (11th month) in the year 104 and day Wahrām (20th day)
               <lb n="29" xml:id="trans-p1-l29"/>he ordered to make.—
               <lb n="30" xml:id="trans-p1-l30"/>C1 To thousand-fold remembered very honoured brother Xradzād, reverence!
               <lb n="31" xml:id="trans-p1-l32"/>C2 Windād-Xw aršēd, the Parišwārgar rad. 
            </ab>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
</TEI>